  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{2}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196134/assets/53ca2220480be7f22b42f8e18df615295868408d7e2b7858c5dd2b17656b1ba8.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{4}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196134/assets/8e4d072f17abd83c86c3c2ba9ea3fec409a01666ec1f96e6b5c16a7e744d597e.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
